      "speaker": null,
      "text": "25 δύναται GE p. 156, #177.\n25–26 οἱ μέν ... οἱ δέ ... ‘some ... others ...’\n27–30 A rather touching personal view. It shows Aristophanes’ sympathy with ‘honest country folk’, and a glimpse of the pre-war Athens.\n32 ἂν βουλοίμην ἄν + optative again – ‘could’, ‘would’.\nἀναπείσω What verb does this come from? Try πείθω.\n33 εἶμι (not εἰμί) ‘I shall go’.\n34 ἄλλο τι πλήν ... ‘anything else but ...’\n42–44 Note ἄν + optative repeatedly.\nPage 97\n46 A quotation from Homer, Odyssey 1.267.\n48–49 Two lines from the Homeric Hymn to Demeter 216–217. The vocabulary should give you all the help you need.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 2,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        190,
        401,
        363
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Translation for 8C",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 3,
      "bbox": [
        413,
        87,
        482,
        804
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "DIKAIOPOLIS",
      "text": "You seem to speak the truth, Peisetairos. But who will save the city, since the orators seem to be worth nothing? Perhaps the people themselves?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 4,
      "bbox": [
        447,
        88,
        480,
        855
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "EUELPIDES",
      "text": "O Herakles, don’t say that! For the people are most skilled at home, but absolute idiots in the assembly.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        486,
        88,
        501,
        337
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAPSODE",
      "text": "But if Pericles –",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        507,
        88,
        521,
        405
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "DIK.",
      "text": "Don’t speak of Pericles!",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        526,
        88,
        559,
        879
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAP.",
      "text": "What do you mean, my friend? Pericles seemed to be the best of them all, so they say.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        564,
        88,
        597,
        796
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "PEISETAIROS",
      "text": "But the good citizen makes the citizens better instead of worse. Did Pericles do this or not?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        603,
        88,
        618,
        303
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAP.",
      "text": "He did it, by Zeus!",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        622,
        88,
        655,
        882
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "PEI.",
      "text": "When Pericles began to speak in the assembly, therefore, were the Athenians worse, and when he died were they better?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 11,
      "bbox": [
        661,
        88,
        694,
        789
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAP.",
      "text": "It is probable that they were. For the good citizen makes the others better.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 12,
      "bbox": [
        700,
        88,
        775,
        893
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "PEI.",
      "text": "But we know clearly, you and I, that at first Pericles was well thought of when the Athenians were, as you say, worse; but when they became better, because of him, they condemned him for theft, and it is clear that he was a villain.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 13,
      "bbox": [
        781,
        88,
        815,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "DIK.",
      "text": "You speak the truth, I know it well. Who will save the city? A man who loves the city will save it and not destroy it. What must we do?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 14,
      "bbox": [
        820,
        88,
        834,
        617
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAP.",
      "text": "Dikaiopolis, you must seek the good of the city.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 15,
      "bbox": [
        839,
        88,
        874,
        901
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "DIK.",
      "text": "But what is the good, rhapsode? For I don’t know what it is that is the good [of the city].",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 16,
      "bbox": [
        880,
        88,
        913,
        874
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "RHAP.",
      "text": "You don’t know what ‘the good’ is? But on the ship you seemed to be some sort of a philosopher, knowing their jargon.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 17,
      "bbox": [
        918,
        88,
        951,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "DIK.",
      "text": "Don’t mock me, rhapsode! For the philosophers search, as I hear, for ‘the good’, but no one can discover it. Some think that it is virtue, and others think",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    }
  ],
